cemc-csmc-2014-a6.body:
Every even locker must differ from every odd locker, so the colours used on the 5 even lockers and on the 5 odd lockers are disjoint sets. They can't be $2 + 2$ (only 3 colours), so the possibilities are:

- one colour each: $3 \times 2 = 6$ ways;
- one colour on the evens ($3$ choices), the other two both used on the odds: $2^5 - 2 = 30$ ways, so $90$;
- the reverse: $90$.

Total $6 + 90 + 90 = 186$.

**Answer: 186**
